{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "3b91928e82204a15b7318c946da513e6",
    "m_Title": "Transform Flow Vectors",
    "m_Content": "Our flow vectors are baked by B2U as 16-bit X and Y properties relative to the mesh normal (this is tangent space!). Because we don't actually have a proper unwrapped UV map, Unity cannot generate mesh tangents for our object. Instead we use this function to caculate the mesh tangents on the fly using the cross product of our object space normal and one of the major world axes. We then use these constructed tangents to transform our baked flow vectors from tangent space to world space. Using the absolute distance baked into the mesh and the materials viscosity, we can also generate the magnitude of our flow vectors for scaling how quickly the fluid is flowing.",
